OLD_SECTION
(no file)

NEW_SECTION
The guide to the core: how the core loads (any vUX import, core.css about 300ms later,
globals by design), the selector rule for $$.sm() (writers act on every match, readers on
the first, no match throws), then selecting, every $$.sm() manipulator grouped by purpose,
slide/flip/animate/filter in detail, attachEventHandler, data and network, time,
environment, the built-in extensions, the global helpers, the error list, and a table of
known defects.

REASON
The core had no guide. doc/README.md said "importing any component boots the vUX core and
its global helpers" but nothing documented $$ itself. Every claim about behaviour was
checked in headless Chromium against the current working tree, which includes the
uncommitted slide-fixes changes, before it was written down. The known-defects table
records what is broken without fixing it: the task was documentation, and each defect
is a separate decision for the maintainer.
